# TR10 Magic technology file (drawing-layer 1um CMOS, 2-metal).
# Layers follow the TR-1um drawing-layer GDS table:
#   AP 3/1  P+ active      AN 3/2  N+ active      AR 3/3 active (raw)
#   GC 8/1  gate poly     SG 8/0  short gate     GR 8/2  poly resistor
#   CO 11/0 contact        M1 13/0 metal1        V1 19/0 via1
#   M2 20/0 metal2        WN 140/0 N-well       NW 36/0 deep N-well marker
#   PM 35/0 P-well marker  NM 7/0 N-well marker  NF 25/0 N+ field
#   PF 26/0 P+ field       prBoundary 235/0
#
# Purpose: GDS streamout (cifoutput) and basic Magic view of TR-1um drawing
# layouts. Full DRC/LVS remain in KLayout runsets (run.drc / run.lvs).

puts stdout "Sourcing TR10 Magic extraction technology..."
if {[tech name] != "TR10"} {
    tech load [file join [file dirname [file normalize [info script]]] TR10.tech]
}
if {[tech name] != "TR10"} {quit -noprompt}
drc on
catch {random seed}
ext2spice scale off
ext2spice cthresh 0
ext2spice rthresh 0
snap lambda

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Parasitic resistance extraction options (magic >= 8.3.597)
#
# `extresist threshold` is a cutoff in MILLIOHMS on the lumped node
# resistance: only nodes above it get a detailed resistor network.  The
# default is 10 ohm, which silently drops every on-chip metal segment,
# leaving the netlist with zero resistors.  Set it to 0 so all nodes are
# considered, and lower `minresist` so short segments are not pruned out of
# the network.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
catch {extresist threshold 0}
catch {extresist minresist 0}
